// BT-3903 (ADR 0133 Phase 1): an actor collection with only `do:`, sent the
// collection messages with a writing block from outside (another process).
// It does not use adr0133enumerable_walkable.bt: inside an actor's own
// method, `self do:` with a writing block drops the write today (BT-3918,
// pinned by `selfDoSum`), which is why the stdlib's `Enumerable` is built on
// `elements` instead (BT-3580). Driven by adr0133enumerable_user.bt.

Actor subclass: Adr0133EnumerableActor
  state: items = #()

  do: block => self.items do: block

  selfDoSum =>
    t := 0
    self do: [:x | t := t + x]
    t
